  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Humanitarian Assistance for Displaced and Conflict-Affected Populations in Plateau State</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Based on data available from the Plateau State Emergency Management Agency (PLASEMA) and the Rapid Needs Assessmemt of Bassa, Barkin Ladi and Riyom , women, young boys and girls are the most vulnerable of the affected population in temporary shelters and unofficial camps. The most critical needs identified include protection services, food/non-food items, and WASH.&#xa0;
The proposed project will address the identified needs through the provision of protection services, unconditional cash transfer, and distribution of dignity kits, WaSH kits.The project will reach about 11,964 project beneficiaries within a 45-day implementation timeframe with these essential services.</narrative>
  </description>
